* BASELINE - Rev B POWER BOARD AS BUILT (Nov 2024) - why it cannot reach its own full scale
* One of the two identical channels.  U3 = LMV358 powered from +4.096 V (REF5040) -> gate can never exceed ~4.1 V.\nIRF530 VGS(th) is 2-4 V (datasheet) and the 0.1 R source resistor needs another 0.3-0.6 V, so the\nreachable current depends on which IRF530 you got.  Op-amp = ideal rail-to-rail proxy (best case for LMV358).
* VSEN amplifier as drawn: R1 (feedback) goes to the\nNON-inverting input and R4 to the inverting input.\nPositive feedback -> output latches to a rail.\nCorrect: swap the R1 and R4 connections.
.param Vdut=12 vth=3
.model IRF530_VTH VDMOS(Rg=3 Vto={vth} Rd=50m Rs=12m Rb=60m Kp=5 lambda=.01 Cgdmax=1n Cgdmin=.26n Cgs=.2n Cjo=.4n Is=52p ksubthres=.1 Vds=100)
.step param vth list 2 3 4   ; IRF530 VGS(th) min / mid / max
.dc Vctrl 0 4.096 8m
.meas DC I_FS FIND Id(Q1) AT 4.096
.meas DC I_target PARAM 4.096*12/80/0.1
.meas DC Vgate_FS FIND V(gate) AT 4.096
.meas DC VSEN_out FIND V(VSEN) AT 2
.meas DC VSEN_correct PARAM 0.1*12
* Library below included based on ModelFile attribute of instance X§U3A, X§U1B (C:\users\crossover\AppData\Local\LTspice\lib\sym\OpAmps\UniversalOpAmp2.asy)
.lib UniversalOpAmp2.lib
.backanno
.end
